## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics

The required script was run, but the configured OpenRouter key had exhausted its total limit.  Every
call returned HTTP 403, and `harden.py` correctly refused to score an API error as an unsolved model
attempt.  Consequently there is **no hardened verdict** and the result is not submission-ready.

| Arm | Preset | Script records | Scored solved/attempts | Result |
|---|---|---:|---:|---|
| bare | easy | 4 redraws | 0/0 | all HTTP 403; no verdict |
| structural hint | easy | 4 redraws | 0/0 | all HTTP 403; unrun diagnostic |
| placebo hint | easy | 4 redraws | 0/0 | all HTTP 403; unrun diagnostic |

`hinted - placebo` is therefore undefined, not evidence of zero effect.  The JSON report stores 0/0 and
`hinted_verdict="unrun"`; the three script-owned transcripts preserve the failures.  Once quota is
restored, rerun all three arms and replace those records before submission.

## Use

```python
import random
import gen_2005_06046 as g

