codex
Implemented a verified Track B generator based on Section 3.1 and Theorem 3.8 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06046).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2005_06046.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/gen_2005_06046.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2005.06046/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All internal gates pass. Notable measurements:

- Exact shipping density: approximately `2.404×10^-76`
- Random guesses: `0/200,000`
- Five no-tool attacks: `0/8` each
- Sturm reference: `87,876` average exact operations, `8/8`
- Paper’s cyclic scan: `4,320,396` operations, `8/8`
- Compact structural route: at most `66` operations
- Answer: `217` characters, `36` atoms

The sole remaining blocker is external: all three oracle runs received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded,” so no attempts were scored and no hardened verdict exists. The error transcripts are preserved honestly; this result is not submission-ready until the OpenRouter quota is restored and the three runs are repeated.
