The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06046) makes circle instances polynomial-time solvable, so the module correctly declares Track B. All internal gates pass, including 0/200,000 random guesses, five failing attacks across eight seeds, exact verification, canonicalization, and G9(c)’s size limits.

The oracle evidence is negative:

- Easy: solved by 2/3 calls.
- Medium: solved by its first call.
- Then OpenRouter returned repeated HTTP 403 “key limit exceeded.”
- Hard was not reached; hinted and placebo arms remain unscored.

The harness therefore produced no terminal `hardened` or `too_easy` verdict. I preserved the genuine successes and errors and explicitly marked the result non-submission-ready. Once quota is restored, the bare loop must be rerun to completion, followed by both G9 arms.
